# A traveller books a ferry and cancels it again, in Island Hop.
# Payments are off on a local backend (no PAYMENTS_ENABLED), so a booking is confirmed straight
# away and nothing is charged. The traveller is a seeded account (prisma/seed.ts).
# Each test books its own test trip, so it never depends on the seeded timetable.
# A trip that was booked can only be cancelled, never deleted, so it stays behind (cancelled).
# That is why the booked one is on Samantha II on its own day: the tests that pick the
# "Royal Alpha" row on the operator's timetable (310 days ahead) never see it.

Test: A traveller books two seats and cancels the booking

  Given a test trip to book on "Samantha II" from "Blowing Point, Anguilla" to "Marigot, Saint Martin", 10:00 to 10:25, in 301 days

  As traveller:
    go to "/ferries?from=Blowing Point, Anguilla&to=Marigot, Saint Martin&departureDate={in 301 days}&adults=2&passengers=2 Passengers"
    click "Select Trip"
    click "Continue to Passenger Details"
    click "Continue to Payment"
    click "Continue to pay"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/bookings
    backend should reply 201 Created
    click "Manage booking"
    click "Cancel Booking"
    in "Cancel Booking" dialog, click "Confirm Cancellation"
    backend should receive PATCH /api/v1/bookings/:id/cancel
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Booking cancelled successfully"


# Two people at once: the traveller gets as far as paying, then the operator cancels the trip.
# The trip is a test trip in 310 days, deleted again when the test ends.
Test: A trip cancelled while the traveller is paying can't be booked

  Given a test trip on "Royal Alpha" from "Blowing Point, Anguilla" to "Marigot, Saint Martin", 10:00 to 10:25, in 310 days

  As traveller:
    go to "/ferries?from=Blowing Point, Anguilla&to=Marigot, Saint Martin&departureDate={in 310 days}&adults=2&passengers=2 Passengers"
    click "Select Trip"
    click "Continue to Passenger Details"
    click "Continue to Payment"

  As operator:
    go to schedules page
    type "{in 310 days}" in "Filter by date"
    in "Royal Alpha" row, choose "Cancelled" for "Change status"
    backend should receive PATCH /api/v1/operator/schedules/:id/status
    backend should reply 200 OK

  As traveller:
    click "Continue to pay"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/bookings
    backend should reply 400 Bad Request
    should see "Cannot book tickets on a departed or cancelled trip"
